## 🚨 Common Pitfalls & Solutions

### Pitfall 1: Module Import Failures
**Wrong**: Trying to import CLI classes directly
```powershell
# ❌ This often fails
@'
import { OptlyCLI } from './src/cli/OptlyCLI.js';
const cli = new OptlyCLI();
'@ | node
```

**Right**: Execute via command line
```powershell
# ✅ This works reliably
@'
const { execSync } = require('child_process');
const result = execSync('node ./bin/optly health', { encoding: 'utf8' });
console.log(result);
'@ | node
```

### Pitfall 2: Quote Escaping Hell
**Wrong**: Complex nested quotes
```powershell
# ❌ Syntax nightmare
node -e "console.log(JSON.stringify({\"test\": \"value with \\\"quotes\\\"\"}))"
```

**Right**: Here-string simplicity
```powershell
# ✅ Clean and readable
@'
console.log(JSON.stringify({"test": "value with \"quotes\""}));
'@ | node
```

### Pitfall 3: Interactive Command Hanging
**Wrong**: Commands that wait for input
```powershell
# ❌ This hangs terminal
node ./bin/optly interactive
```

**Right**: Non-interactive testing
```powershell
# ✅ Test help and status instead
@'
const { execSync } = require('child_process');
console.log(execSync('node ./bin/optly --help', { encoding: 'utf8' }));
'@ | node
```

